Lab 5.B — DNS
The server VM acts as the DNS resolver.
Install Unbound
sudo apt update
sudo apt install unbound dnsutils -y

Enable Unbound
sudo systemctl enable --now unbound

Configure Unbound
sudo nano /etc/unbound/unbound.conf.d/lab.conf

Add:
server:
interface: 10.10.10.1
interface: 10.10.20.1
access-control: 10.10.10.0/24 allow
access-control: 10.10.20.0/24 allow
local-zone: "lab.local." static
local-data: "router.lab.local. IN A 10.10.10.1"
local-data: "ubuntu.lab.local. IN A 10.10.10.20"
local-data: "rocky.lab.local. IN A 10.10.20.20"

Check and restart
sudo unbound-checkconf
sudo systemctl restart unbound

Test DNS
dig @10.10.10.1 example.com

Expected:
status: NOERROR

Configure Ubuntu VM DNS
Netplan:
nameservers:
addresses:
- 10.10.10.1

sudo netplan apply

resolvectl status

Configure Rocky VM DNS
sudo nmcli connection modify "CONNECTION-NAME" ipv4.dns "10.10.20.1"
sudo nmcli connection up "CONNECTION-NAME"

resolvectl status

Cache test
dig @10.10.10.1 example.com

dig @10.10.10.1 example.com

Compare:
;; Query time: XXX msec

The second query should be faster because the answer
is cached by Unbound.
Local names
dig @10.10.10.1 ubuntu.lab.local

dig @10.10.20.1 rocky.lab.local

Expected:
ubuntu.lab.local → 10.10.10.20
rocky.lab.local → 10.10.20.20

Three DNS failures
A. Wrong resolver address
dig @10.10.99.1 example.com

Symptom: timeout
Cause: wrong DNS address
Fix: use 10.10.10.1 / 10.10.20.1
B. Access-control refusal
dig @10.10.10.1 example.com

Symptom: status: REFUSED
Cause: client subnet not allowed
Fix:
access-control: 10.10.10.0/24 allow
access-control: 10.10.20.0/24 allow

C. Stale /etc/hosts
getent hosts ubuntu.lab.local
dig ubuntu.lab.local

Symptom: wrong IP from getent
Cause: stale /etc/hosts entry
Fix: remove or correct the entry
DNS packet capture
sudo tcpdump -i enp0s9 -n port 53

Then run from Rocky:
dig example.com

Shows DNS query and response.
Final proof
sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward

dig @10.10.10.1 example.com

dig @10.10.10.1 ubuntu.lab.local

dig @10.10.20.1 rocky.lab.local
